export const pgUnit02CommonInfoMarkdown: LocalizedText = {
  "en": "# PG Unit 2: My Family, Friends and Home — Common Info\n\n## 1. Unit Theme Overview\n\nPG Unit 2: My Family, Friends and Home helps children connect school life with their most familiar relationships and living spaces. The unit focuses on close family members, friends, home, simple home objects, and early pretend-care routines.\n\nThis unit extends Unit 1’s classroom participation language into more personal and relational contexts. Children begin with familiar people such as mum, dad, baby, teacher, and friend, then move toward simple home routines such as bed, sleep, go home, give Mum the toy, and put Baby in bed.\n\nFor PG children, this unit should be grounded in photos, dolls, puppets, toy homes, soft toys, home-corner play, and real classroom care routines. The purpose is not to require children to name family members verbally or produce relationship sentences. Children may show understanding by looking, touching, pointing, holding, matching, giving, moving dolls or objects, pretending to sleep, or joining teacher-modelled home routines.\n\n## 2. Unit Language\n\n### PG Core Vocabulary\n\n```text\nmum ｜ dad ｜ baby ｜ friend ｜ teacher ｜ home ｜ room ｜ bed ｜ toy ｜ book ｜ bag\n```\n\n### Functional Classroom and Pretend-Play Chunks\n\n```text\nShow me Mum. ｜ Show me Dad. ｜ Point to Mum. ｜ Point to Dad. ｜ This is Mum. ｜ This is Dad. ｜ This is Baby. ｜ This is my friend. ｜ Home. ｜ Go home. ｜ Bed. ｜ Sleep. ｜ Put Baby in bed. ｜ Give Mum the toy. ｜ Give Dad the book. ｜ Bye-bye, Mum. ｜ Bye-bye, Dad.\n```\n\n## 3. Weekly Subthemes\n\n### Week 1: Mum, Dad and Baby\n\nChildren begin with the most familiar family people: mum, dad, and baby. The focus is recognition and emotional connection through photos, puppets, dolls, songs, and simple pointing or showing routines.\n\n### Week 2: My Friend and My Teacher\n\nChildren connect family language with classroom relationship language. The focus is recognising teacher and friend, sitting near peers, passing objects, using soft toys or puppets for social routines, and experiencing the class as a safe group.\n\n### Week 3: Home, Room and Bed\n\nChildren begin to explore simple home spaces and routines through dolls, doll beds, blocks, home-corner play, and soft props. The focus is moving objects into a home space, putting baby in bed, pretending to sleep, and connecting home words with actions.\n\n### Week 4: Family, Home and Goodbye Routine\n\nChildren integrate family, friend, and home routines through short pretend-play sequences: family comes home, baby sleeps, friend visits, toys go home, and people say bye-bye. The focus is emotional security, object return, and repeated relational routines.\n\n## 4. Teacher Input Pool\n\n### Family and Relationship Input\n\nmum ｜ dad ｜ mummy ｜ daddy ｜ baby ｜ friend ｜ teacher ｜ family ｜ this is Mum ｜ this is Dad ｜ this is Baby ｜ my friend\n\n### Home and Object Input\n\nhome ｜ room ｜ bed ｜ toy ｜ book ｜ bag ｜ doll ｜ house ｜ blanket ｜ basket ｜ go home ｜ in bed ｜ sleep\n\n### Action and Routine Input\n\nshow ｜ point ｜ touch ｜ give ｜ take ｜ hold ｜ put ｜ go ｜ sleep ｜ wait ｜ bye-bye ｜ all done ｜ clean up\n\n### Teacher Routine Language\n\nShow me Mum. ｜ Show me Dad. ｜ Point to Mum. ｜ Touch Baby. ｜ Give Mum the toy. ｜ Give Dad the book. ｜ Put Baby in bed. ｜ Baby sleeps. ｜ Go home. ｜ Bye-bye, Mum. ｜ Bye-bye, Dad. ｜ Put it here. ｜ All done. ｜ Good job.\n\n## 5. Expected PG Response Modes\n\nChildren may respond by looking at a family photo, touching a picture, pointing to Mum or Dad, holding a baby doll, giving an object to a doll or puppet, putting Baby in bed, pretending to sleep, waving bye-bye, moving a figure toward a home space, matching a family picture, sitting near a friend, passing a soft toy, or joining a short pretend routine with adult support.\n\nChildren are not expected to name family members independently, answer `Who’s this?` verbally, produce `This is my...`, describe family members, distinguish all extended family roles, name rooms independently, or use full relationship sentences.\n\n## 6. Theme Songs / Chants\n\n### Core Songs\n\nMy Teddy Bear  \nPeekaboo  \nPeekaboo Playground  \nHide And Seek  \nPeekaboo, I Love You  \nBaby Shark  \nThe More We Get Together  \nI Like You  \nSkidamarink  \nSay Cheese!  \nOld MacDonald Had A Farm  \nWhere Is Baby\n\n### Use of Songs\n\nSongs should be used to support emotional connection, turn-taking, hiding-and-finding routines, family roles, friendship, and home-like comfort. Children may listen, look, wave, hide and reveal, hold a teddy, rock a baby doll, move like a family character, or copy one repeated gesture. Singing is optional and not required for PG baseline participation.\n\n## 7. Resource Opportunities\n\n### Useful EASTIE Spaces\n\nClassroom  \nHome corner / pretend-play area  \nSmall outdoor grass area attached to PG classroom  \nTheatre / small dramatic play space  \nArt classroom  \nConstruction / block room  \nBook corner  \nCircle-time area / mat area\n\n### Useful Materials\n\nFamily photo cards  \nTeacher-prepared family picture cards  \nDolls / baby dolls  \nDoll beds  \nDoll strollers  \nBlankets  \nToy kitchen or home-corner materials  \nDollhouse furniture  \nSoft toys  \nTeddy bears  \nPuppets / finger puppets  \nBags  \nBooks  \nBaskets  \nToy food  \nLarge wooden blocks  \nLego bricks  \nCloths / scarves / covering fabric  \nVisual routine cards  \nName cards or child photos\n\n### Enhanced Resource Opportunities\n\nA class family wall or photo basket can help children connect home and school in a safe way. Doll beds, blankets, and baby-care props can support repeated bed/sleep/home routines. Construction materials can be used to build simple home spaces for dolls and soft toys. Puppets and teddies can help children participate in family and friend routines without pressure to speak.\n\n## 8. Boundary Notes\n\nThis unit should not become a formal family-tree unit. PG children do not need to identify extended family members, explain relationships, or describe family structure.\n\nThis unit should not require children to speak about their own family on demand. Family and home topics can be emotionally sensitive, especially for very young children. Children may participate through photos, dolls, puppets, and pretend play without verbal disclosure.\n\nThis unit should not teach full relationship sentences as required output. `This is my mum.` and `This is my dad.` may appear in teacher modelling or later PK optional challenge, but PG baseline participation remains non-verbal and action-based.\n\nThis unit should not overload children with many room names or home objects. PG focus remains on the most concrete and emotionally familiar items: mum, dad, baby, friend, teacher, home, room, bed, toy, book, and bag.\n\n## 9. Unit-Level Observation Focus\n\nTeachers observe whether children begin to recognise familiar family and relationship words, respond to photos or dolls through looking and touching, participate in simple home and baby-care routines, show comfort with friend and teacher language, join pretend play involving home or bed, wave or respond to bye-bye routines, and use objects to represent people and places.\n\nObservation should focus on emotional connection, symbolic participation, relational awareness, pretend-play readiness, and action-based comprehension rather than spoken family vocabulary output.\n",
  "zh": "# PG Unit 2: My Family, Friends and Home — Common Info｜PG 单元 2：我的家人、朋友与家 — 通用信息\n\n## 1. Unit Theme Overview｜单元主题概览\n\nPG 单元 2：我的家人、朋友与家帮助儿童把学校生活与他们最熟悉的人际关系和生活空间连接起来。本单元聚焦于亲近的家人、朋友、家、简单的家中物品以及早期的假装照护常规。\n\n本单元把单元 1 的课堂参与语言延伸到更个人化和关系性的情境中。儿童从最熟悉的人开始——妈妈、爸爸、宝宝、教师、朋友——然后过渡到简单的家庭常规，例如床、睡觉、回家、把玩具给妈妈、把宝宝放进床里。\n\n对于 PG 儿童，本单元应扎根于照片、娃娃、木偶、玩具家、软玩具、家庭角游戏，以及真实的课堂照护常规。目的不是要求儿童口头命名家庭成员或产出关系句。儿童可以通过看、触摸、指、拿、匹配、给予、移动娃娃或物品、假装睡觉，或加入教师示范的家庭常规来展示理解。\n\n## 2. Unit Language｜单元语言\n\n### PG Core Vocabulary｜PG 核心词汇\n\nmum ｜ dad ｜ baby ｜ friend ｜ teacher ｜ home ｜ room ｜ bed ｜ toy ｜ book ｜ bag\n\n### Functional Classroom and Pretend-Play Chunks｜实用课堂与假装游戏句块\n\nShow me Mum. ｜ Show me Dad. ｜ Point to Mum. ｜ Point to Dad. ｜ This is Mum. ｜ This is Dad. ｜ This is Baby. ｜ This is my friend. ｜ Home. ｜ Go home. ｜ Bed. ｜ Sleep. ｜ Put Baby in bed. ｜ Give Mum the toy. ｜ Give Dad the book. ｜ Bye-bye, Mum. ｜ Bye-bye, Dad.\n\n## 3. Weekly Subthemes｜周次子主题\n\n### Week 1: Mum, Dad and Baby｜第一周：妈妈、爸爸和宝宝\n\n儿童从最熟悉的家人开始：妈妈、爸爸和宝宝。重点是通过照片、木偶、娃娃、歌曲和简单的指或展示常规来建立识别与情感连接。\n\n### Week 2: My Friend and My Teacher｜第二周：我的朋友和我的老师\n\n儿童把家庭语言与课堂关系语言连接起来。重点是识别教师和朋友、坐在同伴附近、传递物品、用软玩具或木偶进行社交常规，以及体验班级作为一个安全的集体。\n\n### Week 3: Home, Room and Bed｜第三周：家、房间和床\n\n儿童通过娃娃、娃娃床、积木、家庭角游戏和软道具开始探索简单的家庭空间和常规。重点是把物品移入家庭空间、把宝宝放进床里、假装睡觉，并把家的词汇与动作连接起来。\n\n### Week 4: Family, Home and Goodbye Routine｜第四周：家庭、家与再见常规\n\n儿童通过简短的假装游戏序列把家庭、朋友和家的常规整合起来：家人回家、宝宝睡觉、朋友来访、玩具回家、大家说再见。重点是情感安全感、物品归位和重复的关系性常规。\n\n## 4. Teacher Input Pool｜教师输入库\n\n### Family and Relationship Input｜家庭与关系输入\n\nmum ｜ dad ｜ mummy ｜ daddy ｜ baby ｜ friend ｜ teacher ｜ family ｜ this is Mum ｜ this is Dad ｜ this is Baby ｜ my friend\n\n### Home and Object Input｜家与物品输入\n\nhome ｜ room ｜ bed ｜ toy ｜ book ｜ bag ｜ doll ｜ house ｜ blanket ｜ basket ｜ go home ｜ in bed ｜ sleep\n\n### Action and Routine Input｜动作与常规输入\n\nshow ｜ point ｜ touch ｜ give ｜ take ｜ hold ｜ put ｜ go ｜ sleep ｜ wait ｜ bye-bye ｜ all done ｜ clean up\n\n### Teacher Routine Language｜教师常规语言\n\nShow me Mum. ｜ Show me Dad. ｜ Point to Mum. ｜ Touch Baby. ｜ Give Mum the toy. ｜ Give Dad the book. ｜ Put Baby in bed. ｜ Baby sleeps. ｜ Go home. ｜ Bye-bye, Mum. ｜ Bye-bye, Dad. ｜ Put it here. ｜ All done. ｜ Good job.\n\n## 5. Expected PG Response Modes｜预期 PG 反应方式\n\n儿童可能通过以下方式反应：看家庭照片、触摸一张图片、指妈妈或爸爸、抱着一个娃娃、把物品给娃娃或木偶、把宝宝放进床里、假装睡觉、挥手说再见、把一个小人偶移向家庭空间、匹配一张家庭照片、坐在朋友附近、传递一个软玩具，或在成人支持下加入一个简短的假装常规。\n\n不要求儿童独立命名家庭成员、口头回答\"这是谁？\"、产出\"This is my...\"、描述家庭成员、区分所有大家庭角色、独立命名房间，或使用完整的关系句。\n\n## 6. Core Unit Songs｜单元核心歌曲\n\n### Core Songs｜核心歌曲\n\nMy Teddy Bear  \nPeekaboo  \nPeekaboo Playground  \nHide And Seek  \nPeekaboo, I Love You  \nBaby Shark  \nThe More We Get Together  \nI Like You  \nSkidamarink  \nSay Cheese!  \nOld MacDonald Had A Farm  \nWhere Is Baby\n\n### Use of Songs｜歌曲的使用\n\n歌曲应当用来支持情感连接、轮流、躲藏与发现常规、家庭角色、友谊以及家一般的舒适感。儿童可以听、看、挥手、躲藏和揭示、抱着泰迪、摇一个娃娃、像家庭角色一样移动，或模仿一个重复的手势。歌唱是可选项，并非 PG 基线参与的必需。\n\n## 7. Resource Opportunities｜资源机会\n\n### Useful EASTIE Spaces｜可用 EASTIE 空间\n\nClassroom  \nHome corner / pretend-play area  \nSmall outdoor grass area attached to PG classroom  \nTheatre / small dramatic play space  \nArt classroom  \nConstruction / block room  \nBook corner  \nCircle-time area / mat area\n\n### Useful Materials｜可用材料\n\nFamily photo cards  \nTeacher-prepared family picture cards  \nDolls / baby dolls  \nDoll beds  \nDoll strollers  \nBlankets  \nToy kitchen or home-corner materials  \nDollhouse furniture  \nSoft toys  \nTeddy bears  \nPuppets / finger puppets  \nBags  \nBooks  \nBaskets  \nToy food  \nLarge wooden blocks  \nLego bricks  \nCloths / scarves / covering fabric  \nVisual routine cards  \nName cards or child photos\n\n### Enhanced Resource Opportunities｜拓展资源机会\n\n班级家庭墙或照片篮可以帮助儿童把家和学校以安全的方式连接起来。娃娃床、毛毯和宝宝照护道具可以支持重复的床／睡觉／家常规。建构材料可以用来为娃娃和软玩具搭建简单的家庭空间。木偶和泰迪可以帮助儿童在没有说话压力的情况下参与家庭和朋友的常规。\n\n## 8. Boundary Notes｜边界说明\n\n本单元不应变成正式的家谱单元。PG 儿童不需要识别大家庭成员、解释关系，或描述家庭结构。\n\n本单元不应要求儿童按需谈论自己的家庭。家庭和家的话题可能情感敏感，尤其是对非常年幼的儿童。儿童可以通过照片、娃娃、木偶和假装游戏来参与，无需口头透露。\n\n本单元不应把完整的关系句作为必需输出来教。\"This is my mum.\" 和 \"This is my dad.\" 可以出现在教师示范或后续 PK 可选挑战中，但 PG 基线参与仍然是非语言和动作导向的。\n\n本单元不应让儿童承受过多房间名称或家中物品。PG 重点仍是最具体且情感熟悉的物品：妈妈、爸爸、宝宝、朋友、教师、家、房间、床、玩具、书和包。\n\n## 9. Unit-Level Observation Focus｜单元观察重点\n\n教师观察儿童是否开始识别熟悉的家庭和关系词、通过看和触摸对照片或娃娃做出反应、参与简单的家庭和宝宝照护常规、对朋友和教师语言感到舒适、参与涉及家或床的假装游戏、对再见常规做出挥手或回应，以及用物品代表人或地方。\n\n观察应聚焦于情感连接、象征性参与、关系意识、假装游戏准备度和动作导向的理解，而非口头家庭词汇输出。"
};

